From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:54:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: let an idle USB-C
 port's AON domain power down

With nothing plugged in, macOS 26B123 on the J604 has ATC0_USB_AON,
ATC1_USB_AON and ATC3_USB_AON off (its idle power map: OFF, with the
xHCI at power state 0 of 4), while Linux keeps them on: they were marked
apple,always-on to mirror the J713's apple,inherited-on, which keeps
them on as handed over.

Nothing needs them on while their ports are idle. Each is a parent of
its ATCn_USB domain, which holds the port's controller, DARTs and PHY,
so genpd powers the AON domain up before any of those whenever the port
is used. Plug detection is the Type-C controller's, on another bus. The
PHY already sets its PIPE handler and USB2 PHY up again after its domain
was off (atcphy_restore_after_pd_off()), and the controller starts from
reset. Drop apple,always-on so an idle port's AON domain goes off with
the rest of the port, as on macOS.

ATC2, the HDMI side, keeps its policy.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 63797d1fd6..14e63d49d4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -845,12 +845,10 @@ &ps_debug_switch {
 
 &ps_atc0_usb_aon {
 	status = "okay";
-	apple,always-on;
 };
 
 &ps_atc1_usb_aon {
 	status = "okay";
-	apple,always-on;
 };
 
 &ps_atc0_usb {
@@ -866,9 +864,6 @@ &ps_atc2_usb_aon {
 	apple,always-on;
 };
 
-&ps_atc3_usb_aon {
-	apple,always-on;
-};
 
 &ps_atc2_usb {
 	status = "okay";
